## 1. Overview of the Pāḷi Text
* **Sampajānamusāvāde pācittiyaṃ**: In deliberate false speech, there is an offense involving expiation.
* **Omasavāde pācittiyaṃ**: In insult or verbal assault, there is an offense involving expiation.
* **Bhikkhu pesuññe pācittiyaṃ**: In the backbiting or slandering of a bhikkhu, there is an offense involving expiation.
* **Yo pana bhikkhu anusampannaṃ padaso dhammaṃ vāceyya pācittiyaṃ**: If any bhikkhu should have one who has not been fully admitted recite the Dhamma line by line, there is an offense involving expiation.
* **Yo pana bhikkhu anupasampannena uttaridirattatirattaṃ sahaseyyaṃ kappeyya, pācittiyaṃ**: If any bhikkhu should make use of a sleeping place for more than two or three nights together with one who has not been fully admitted, there is an offense involving expiation.
* **Yo pana bhikkhu anupasampannassa uttarimanussadhammaṃ āroceyya bhūtasmiṃ, pācittiyaṃ**: If any bhikkhu should declare a superhuman state to one who has not been fully admitted, when it is a fact, there is an offense involving expiation.

