## 3. Omasavāda Sikkhāpada (Insulting/Belittling Speech)
> **Rule:** *Omasavāde pācittiyaṃ.* (In insult or verbal assault, there is a case involving expiation.)

### Description & Types
* **What is Omasavāda?** *(Vibhaṅga Exam Topic)*
  The intentional act (**cetanā**) rooted in **anger** (1) of belittling (*omasati*), insulting (*khuṁseti*), or despising (*vambheti*) another (2) done bodily or verbally (3) by using one of the ten *akkosa vatthu* (4).
* **3 Action Types:**
  1. *Omasati* - Belittles (literally, "rubs down").
  2. *Khuṃseti* - Insults.
  3. *Vambheti* - Despises.

